# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets applies "Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate" to
# every static file by default (verified against Cloudflare's own docs) — that's correct for most
# of /public, but wrong for /_next/static/*, whose filenames are content-hashed by Next.js's build
# and therefore safe to cache forever. Without this override, browsers/the CDN would revalidate
# these on every load instead of caching them for a year, unlike Next.js's default behavior on
# other hosts. See https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
